# 🚨 THE FIRST TWO RULES ARE THE IMPORTANT ONES. A ROM or a save state accidentally baked into a
# published image is a copyright problem that cannot be recalled once the layer is on a registry,
# and layers persist even if a later step deletes the file. Belt and braces with .gitignore.
*.gb
*.gbc
*.state
*.state.*

# Checkpoints: large, and never wanted in the image -- the worker fetches the one it needs.
*.zip
candidates/
repo/v2/runs/
runs_meta/

# Secrets. None of these should exist under this tree, but an image build is the wrong place to
# find out otherwise.
.env
*_tokens.json
*cookies.txt

venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
*.bak-*
logs/
music/
frames/
preview/
